# LAB-PROD-3 — Technician Capacity Planning

Read-only **decision-support** for lab technician capacity. Builds on
LAB-PROD-2 (`lab-prod-2-operational-analytics-kpi-go`). Canonical rules:

1. **Decision-support only. NEVER auto-assign** technician/order/branch/external-
   lab/due-date/priority/status/QC. Recommendations are read-only + explainable.
2. **No employee ranking / score / leaderboard.** Only load, capacity,
   availability, capability, due-risk, distribution.
3. **planning_unit is explicit** (`minutes` | `units`); never mix units in one
   plan — mismatched-unit profiles are treated as unconfigured (coverage flag).
4. **Missing profile ⇒ UNCONFIGURED / UNPLANNABLE, never a fake zero.** Zero
   denominator ⇒ `null`/"N/A", never a fake %.
5. Capacity + workload + capability are **effective-dated**; capacity can never
   be negative; overlap is rejected server-side.
6. **Reuse LAB-PROD-2, do not duplicate calculators.** Consume
   `LabOperationalAnalyticsRepositoryInterface::technicianAssignmentStats`
   (historical completion confidence) + `LabWorkflowSlaBaselineService`. SLA/
   deadline stays `trx_lab_orders.due_date` only. V2-only (`workflow_version=2`),
   `max_scan_orders` cap.
7. **Branch scope applies to DEMAND (orders); technicians are lab-wide** (no
   branch column on `mst_technicians`). Owner cross-branch read-only.
8. **Technician own-scope is IDOR-forced** via `mst_technicians.user_id`; a
   forged `technician_id`/`branch_id` is ignored/re-scoped server-side. Sidebar
   is not a security boundary.
9. **No PII** (KTP/NIK/patient/clinical) in any plan/table/recommendation/export.
   CSV export is scope-identical + formula-injection-safe.
10. Architecture: HTTP → Controller (thin) → FormRequest → Service (formulas) →
    RepositoryInterface → Repository (queries) → Model. Config writes are
    transactional (`DB::transaction` + `lockForUpdate`). No query/formula in Blade.
11. Permissions: `view_lab_technician_capacity` (Admin Lab, Owner),
    `view_own_lab_technician_capacity` (Technician), `manage_lab_technician_capacity`
    (Admin Lab config CRUD), `export_lab_technician_capacity`.
12. Gate before GO/deploy: `lab-workflow:technician-capacity-audit --strict` +
    `lab-workflow:technician-capacity-go-no-go --strict` (exit 0 only on GO); no
    fake GO. Additive `mst_lab_*` migrations only; never migrate:fresh/db:wipe.
13. A future capacity-consuming sprint (e.g. LAB-PROD-4) MUST reuse
    `LabTechnicianCapacityPlanningService` + repository + the own tier — never a
    parallel capacity calculator.
